    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bb602286-5a0d-532c-a3d9-c3580defec00",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-10 \\\\ 2x+4y &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -10 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 30\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -3 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-10 \\\\ y &=3,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(3)=-10\\,\u21d2\\,x=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$ and $y=3.$",
